From 97706c40e6b85b016d2c224cf89c22678b61fbb6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 00:24:16 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/6] fix(installer): name a bundle's files by their manifests,
 not the archive

extractBundle wrote each .apk entry under its file name with the folders
dropped, and an installed split was named split_ plus that file name. An
APK set keeps APKs of the same name in different folders (bundletool's
splits/ and standalones/, two variants' base-master.apk and
base-master_2.apk), which collided or were taken as more than one base,
and the installed names followed whatever the archive called its files
(split_base-xxhdpi.apk, split_display.apk) where Android names them
split_<split name>.apk.

Stage every entry under a generated name, read its manifest, and name it
base.apk or split_<split name>.apk (InstalledSplitSet.apkName, the names
PackageInstallerSession already gives session installs), with the .dm
that sat beside it in the archive. No archive path reaches the
filesystem, so an entry can no longer collide with or escape the staging
directory, and a second APK for the same split is reported as such. Loose
companion splits and the unchanged check use the same manifest names.

SplitPackageContractTest expects the manifest-named split paths, and an
APK+ that holds the installed cluster under other entry names is now the
same install ("unchanged").

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_0185vQkPNo1ENZ3Mi9zALKd2
